        "basis": "Derived, not measured. All values are unitless multiples of font-size, rounded up to 0.01, and are the maximum over the measured files. T and B are the measured top and bottom ink extremes above/below the baseline divided by unitsPerEm for a scenario; A and D are ascent and descent of a vertical-metrics set divided by unitsPerEm. stacking = T + B: the baseline distance at which the deepest ink of one line cannot touch the tallest ink of the next. containment = max(2T - (A - D), 2B + (A - D)): the line-height at which ink stays inside its own CSS line box (the baseline sits (L + A - D)/2 below the top of a line box of height L), taken as the maximum over the metric sets a browser may use: hhea, and OS/2 typo when USE_TYPO_METRICS is set, otherwise OS/2 win. ui = containment for unvocalised Arabic letters, both digit sets, Arabic punctuation and Basic Latin (single-line controls clip or abut at the line box). body = stacking for Arabic text carrying at most one tashkeel mark per letter. withTashkeel = stacking for fully vocalised text: shadda plus a vowel above, kasra/kasratan below, as placed by GPOS mark and mkmk at the default master. natural = (hhea.ascender - hhea.descender + hhea.lineGap) / unitsPerEm, what line-height: normal resolves to where hhea is used."
